# Named providers in docs

A provider’s **own** page may name that product. Everywhere else, write the generic rule.

A passing instance is fine: “hosted providers (Supabase) reuse this driver.” Do not make that product the sample, the `id`, or the Related default on a shared page.

## Do

- Use `id: "<product>"` or a made-up id on driver / API / “adding a provider” pages
- Link the product page when the reader should open that provider

## Do not

- Put `id: "supabase"` (or Neon, etc.) in examples on the Postgres or API pages
- Build a generic section around one hosted product

```ts
// Bad — Postgres driver page
postgres({ id: "supabase", connectionString });

// Good
postgres({ id: "<product>", connectionString });
```
